---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/") ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---

<BaseLayout title="PMDD Review" active="pmdd">
  <section class="page-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">PMDD Review</p>
      <h2>Hormonal pattern review</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="soft-copy">This review looks for recurring patterns in symptoms that may be hormonally related and records the intermittent PMDD medication trials. PMDD remains a working hypothesis. The Capacity Timeline shows the wider pattern of fluctuating capacity regardless of cause.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="pmdd-summary" class="summary-grid" aria-live="polite"></section>

  <section class="pmdd-actions">
    <a href={`${base}pmdd/report/`} class="primary-button">Export GP Report</a>
    <button type="button" id="copy-pmdd-summary" class="secondary-button">Copy text summary</button>
    <p id="pmdd-copy-status" class="copy-status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="section-title">
      <div>
        <h3>Mood and capacity pattern</h3>
        <p>This shows whether mood, interest and waking capacity changed together or independently. It does not diagnose or exclude depression.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div id="mood-capacity-pattern" class="plain-panel" aria-live="polite"></div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="section-title">
      <div>
        <h3>Recurring hormonal pattern</h3>
        <p>The most repeated features across episodes marked Yes or Possible. Counts refer to episodes, not individual days.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div id="pmdd-pattern" class="plain-panel" aria-live="polite"></div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="section-title">
      <div>
        <h3>Possible hormonal episodes</h3>
        <p>These begin with the wider Capacity Timeline, then use the separately recorded hormonal relevance.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div id="pmdd-episodes" class="pmdd-episodes" aria-live="polite"></div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="section-title">
      <div>
        <h3>PMDD medication courses</h3>
        <p>Medication courses are shown separately and linked to an episode where their dates overlap.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div id="pmdd-periods" class="pmdd-periods" aria-live="polite"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="plain-panel pmdd-method-note">
    <h3>How this is worked out</h3>
    <p>A possible hormonal episode is a Capacity Episode whose hormonal relevance is Yes or Possible. Medication courses begin with a recorded Yes and end with the first explicit No; missing days remain unknown.</p>
    <p>Medication response compares the three days before a medication start with the following five days using recorded capacity, energy and executive clarity. It also keeps my own judgement separately. Improvement after medication is useful evidence to discuss with my GP, but timing alone cannot prove that medication caused it.</p>
  </section>

  <script src="../scripts/pmdd.ts"></script>
</BaseLayout>
